From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS=1: bound idle IR and scratch; halve descriptor starts

Port of Mihawk 0230 / 70b85df in PS5_Lichii (handle mihawk), off by default.
Our descriptor queues already start at a quarter of upstream (0107): with the
switch they start at half of that (upstream's starts) and grow on demand back
to 0107's size at most, never past it; a refused growth keeps the smaller
payload and the overflow wait as before. Shader IR pools keep at most 4 MiB
(or one base chunk) when squashed; a refused squash leaves the pool as after
Free(). Upload scratch over 8 MiB is freed every 256 frames, the ASTC scan
buffer after a scan over 8 MiB. 0505 (EDEN_UP_IR_FREE*) and
EDEN_TC_SCRATCH_KEEP_MIB stay independent. Unset: all as before.
v2 (review): descriptor ceiling 2x start instead of 32x (draft allowed up to
16x 0107's memory), bad_alloc fallbacks on growth and squash, unreachable
pool branch removed.

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/object_pool.h b/src/shader_recompiler/object_pool.h
index 841c273..1fe6852 100644
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/object_pool.h
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/object_pool.h
@@ -3,9 +3,14 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <memory>
+#include <new>
 #include <type_traits>
 #include <utility>
+#include <vector>
+
+#include "common/pe_switch.h"
 
 namespace Shader {
 
@@ -54,12 +59,29 @@ public:
         if (chunks.empty()) {
             return;
         }
+        // EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS (Mihawk 0230): a squashed root keeps at most 4 MiB (or one base
+        // chunk), so one huge shader does not hold its IR for the session. The old chunks go
+        // first; if the smaller root is refused the pool is left as after Free(), which allocates
+        // nothing and makes a fresh chunk at the next Create.
+        static const bool trim = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS");
         Chunk& root{chunks.front()};
         if (root.used_objects == root.num_objects) {
             // Root chunk has been filled, squash allocations into it
             const size_t total_objects{root.num_objects + new_chunk_size * (chunks.size() - 1)};
-            chunks.clear();
-            chunks.emplace_back(total_objects);
+            if (trim) {
+                const size_t kept{(std::max)(new_chunk_size, (size_t{4} << 20) / sizeof(Storage))};
+                chunks.clear();
+                try {
+                    chunks.emplace_back((std::min)(total_objects, kept));
+                } catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
+                    node = nullptr;
+                    chunks.shrink_to_fit();
+                    return;
+                }
+            } else {
+                chunks.clear();
+                chunks.emplace_back(total_objects);
+            }
         } else {
             root.Release();
             chunks.resize(1);
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_update_descriptor.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_update_descriptor.cpp
index 29f3ee7..d383cff 100644
